/**
@page architecture Architecture drawings

@section components Component dependencies

Arrows mean "calls or imports". The data and numerical layers do not call Qt.
The GUI and CLI share the same import, export and analysis functions.

@dot
 digraph components {
   graph [rankdir=TB, bgcolor="transparent"];
   node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fillcolor="#eef4fb", fontname="sans-serif"];
   edge [fontname="sans-serif"];
   launch [label="BAT / SH launcher\nscripts/launch.py"];
   direct [label="run_opencaliper.py\ncurrent interpreter"];
   cli [label="cli.py\ncommand dispatch"];
   gui [label="gui.py\nQt desktop workspace"];
   workspace [label="workspace.py\nportable archives / undo"];
   tools [label="tools.py\nprocessing dialogs / export"];
   processing [label="processing.py\nsignal operations"];
   converters [label="converterscripts/\nregistry / readers / exporters"];
   core [label="core.py\nSignal / Recording\nload / export"];
   analysis [label="analysis.py\nFFT / statistics / cursors"];
   acquisition [label="acquisition.py\nMAT scaling / waveform writers"];
   raw [label="raw.py\nRAW writer"];
   libraries [label="SciPy / hdf5storage\nasammdf / spicelib"];
   qt [label="PySide6 / pyqtgraph"];
   direct -> gui; launch -> cli; cli -> gui; cli -> core; cli -> analysis;
   gui -> core; gui -> analysis; gui -> qt;
   gui -> workspace; gui -> tools; tools -> processing; processing -> core;
   core -> converters; converters -> acquisition; converters -> raw; converters -> libraries;
   acquisition -> libraries;
 }
@enddot

@section ownership Runtime ownership

The following drawing describes logical state ownership, rather than a complete
Python inheritance diagram. Signal IDs are session-local integers; plots use
them to reference loaded sources. The explorer is shared by all analysis tabs.

@dot
 digraph ownership {
   graph [rankdir=LR, bgcolor="transparent"];
   node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fillcolor="#eef8ee", fontname="sans-serif"];
   window [label="Window\nsource and file registries"];
   explorer [label="MeasurementExplorer\nfile / channel tree"];
   page [label="AnalysisPage (one per tab)\nkind / cursors / A-B placement\nFFT interval / resampling"];
   plot [label="Plot (one per subplot)\ncurves / axes / colors / aliases\nannotations / displayed signals"];
   signal [label="Signal\ntime / values / unit / domain"];
   worker [label="Loader\none file import"];
   window -> explorer [label="owns"];
   window -> page [label="tabs"];
   page -> plot [label="plots"];
   window -> signal [label="source ID registry"];
   plot -> signal [label="time/spectrum: source reference\nFFT: transformed result", style=dashed];
   window -> worker [label="retains until finished"];
 }
@enddot

@section loading Loading and displaying a channel

@dot
 digraph loading {
   graph [rankdir=TB, bgcolor="transparent"];
   node [shape=box, fontname="sans-serif"];
   open [label="Open file / drop local URL"];
   worker [label="Window.open_path -> Loader.run\nworker thread calls core.load"];
   model [label="Recording with physical Signal arrays"];
   registry [label="Qt loaded signal -> Window.loaded\nGUI thread registers IDs and tree items"];
   auto [label="Frequency sources: create Spectrum tab\nand plot detector channels automatically"];
   registry -> auto; auto -> add;
   drag [label="Drag channel ID using internal MIME payload"];
   add [label="Window.add_signal\nresolve source; calculate FFT if needed"];
   display [label="Plot curve and signal sidebar"];
   open -> worker -> model -> registry -> drag -> add -> display;
 }
@enddot

@section boundaries Important boundaries

Import runs in worker threads. FFT, processing, workspace serialization and export
run on the GUI thread. Most formats load into memory; NPY input keeps memory-mapped
backing. Time/FFT plots may downsample for display; imported Spectrum pages retain
nonuniform frequency sweeps. Numerical analysis uses full source arrays.

FFT pages store the source time interval separately from frequency cursors.
Explicit linear resampling supports uneven acquisition times without changing
source arrays. Signal.domain identifies seconds versus Hz while Signal.time
retains the horizontal axis field name. ESRP MAT spectra open without an FFT.

With differential cursors enabled, plain left clicks alternate A/B placement;
drags and right-click menus remain available. Plot-local aliases affect legends,
axis labels and cursor readouts without mutating the source channel name.

GUI "Export all" exports loaded source channels rather than calculated FFT curves.
Portable .ocw archives embed channel arrays and view state. Structural undo retains
array references for up to 50 actions. Saved archives exclude undo history,
processing recipes and transient spectrogram windows. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
and `docs/WORKSPACE_FORMAT.md` for complete behavior and limitations.
*/
